# TypeScript

On conflict, [persistence.mdc](./persistence.mdc), [frontend.mdc](./frontend.mdc), and [docs/ACCOUNTS.md](../../docs/ACCOUNTS.md) win.

## Immutability

Update classroom data immutably — copy, do not mutate `ClassroomDatabase` in place.

## Error handling

Use async/await with try/catch; surface actionable messages. Avoid empty `catch` and silent failures.

## Validation

Zod is **optional** — use only where the feature already does. Prefer existing guards in `database/` and `utils/`.

## Console

Avoid new `console.log` in production paths; use existing logging (`logAppEvent` on desktop).

## Secrets

- Never hardcode API keys, tokens, or passwords
- Worker-only: `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`, D1/R2 in Wrangler bindings
- App: `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` is public at build time — never put secrets there. Rebuild Tauri after `.env.local` changes. OAuth details: [docs/ACCOUNTS.md](../../docs/ACCOUNTS.md)

## XSS

Student/teacher names and user text are untrusted. Do not use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, `.innerHTML`, `insertAdjacentHTML`, `eval`, `new Function`, or `document.write`.

## Worker touchpoints

When editing `workers/cloud-backup`: JWT ownership for R2 prefix, body size limits, no classroom runtime logic on Worker.

## Skip

- API response envelopes (`{ success, data }`)
- Mandatory Zod on every input
